      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T00:10:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "10ms does not work I think; I tested 100ms 100 times and it passed.\n\n\u003eI feel like the quirk would be fairly similar in complexity to implement (rx counters instead of tx counters)\n\nThis is already a quirk; I was just against adding a specific flag for it :)\nOr did you mean something else from:\n\n\u003e Should we add a quirk that delays the first ACL packet from a connection?",
      "parentUuid": "bd53d215_00303f48",
      "revId": "3a6a324979ab6dc0777676da2e9754070a61ba2e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
